1. PURPOSE AND DEFINITIONS

The source is published so that anyone can inspect how tokenstat handles data,
contribute improvements, share source changes, and build and run their own
versions.

"Software" means the material covered by section 2, including copies,
modifications, derivative works, and portions of that material. "You" means
the person or entity exercising permissions under this licence.

"tokenstat" means the Software and the products and services pueev OÜ
publishes from it, under that name or any later name, including successor
and related products. "pueev OÜ" includes its successors and assigns.

"Your organization" means one legal entity and the entities that control it,
are controlled by it or are under common control with it, together with
their employees and individual contractors acting for them. A group that
anyone may join, or whose members are its customers or users, is not Your
organization.

"Source Form" means the preferred form for making modifications, including
human-readable source code, documentation, configuration and build scripts.

"Build" means a compiled, packaged or otherwise prepared executable version
of the Software, or a product containing such a version, including binaries,
libraries, installers, app bundles, APKs, IPAs, container images, firmware,
and compiled or obfuscated web applications. This includes modified versions
and products incorporating only part of the Software. An archive of Source
Form is not a Build merely because it includes scripts that can be run by an
interpreter. Adding source files to a Build does not make it Source Form.

"Store" means any app store or software marketplace, including alternative
app marketplaces, and their beta, preview and testing channels, such as
TestFlight and store test tracks. It also means any package or container
registry, package manager repository or index, and similar catalogue from
which software is installed. It covers them on every platform, whether the
listing is free or paid. A release attachment or continuous integration
artifact of a source repository is not, by itself, a Store.

"Account Functions" means the parts of the Software that handle accounts,
sign-in, authentication, licensing, subscriptions, purchases and entitlement
checks, and their connection to the services operated by pueev OÜ.


